  "visualBrief": "Two street portals, open landings and spiral stairs, upper and lower quarry galleries with five historic stone inscriptions, the quarry workshop with solid-rock and stacked-stone supports, the painted ossuary threshold, the sepulchral lamp and its two painted piers, the guarded Samaritaine well, the September Martyrs’ wall and the Crypt of the Passion. The restored Pillars Hall and stone-pier vestibule connect the upper quarry to the ossuary. A short straight flight and lower spiral extend the Fontis event-route vestibule in the near levels. The documented renovated hague has a separate pale limestone footing, an irregular bone face and a ragged upper edge. The stop 7 plaque has a scalloped limestone tablet over a flared pedestal, with carved verse and skulls beside the foot in the near view. The guided-route Sacellum chamber has a stepped limestone altar, three tablets and a return lined with bone courses. The René-Coty spiral opens into a side room and a short level crossing to the central street passage. The eastern ossuary gallery links the northern junction to the Crypt of the Passion passage through open, level mouths. The former Fontis street exit has a single recessed door, a triangular lintel hood and a zinc eave fitted to the low PMTiles footprint. Its upper spiral reaches local grade in the draft. The exit-side gallery bends toward the René-Coty stair beside a distinct junction to the guided Fontis gallery.",
  "nativeAxes": "+X east, +Y up, +Z south. Origin at the centre of the Denfert-Rochereau pavilion.",
